\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O'er the harvest reaped or lost
\par Falls the eve; our tasks are over:
\par Purpose crowned or purpose crossed
\par None may mar and none recover,
\par Now, O merciful and just,
\par Trembling lay we  down the trust;
\par Slender fruit of thriftless day,
\par Father, at thy feet we lay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Yea, but Thou, O Judge and Lord,
\par Yea, but Thou, O strong and holy,
\par Take, and in Thy bosom stored,
\par By Thy pure hands changing wholly,
\par Turn to gold the things of naught,
\par Falling deed and falling thought:
\par Love, how faint, yet love, we give;
\par Thou within Thee make it live.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Gracious task our heart shall bear
\par Now for sweeter call has found us:
\par Airs of home and days that were
\par Wind re-woven chains around us;
\par By the hearthstone, whence we came,
\par Love shall trim her gentle flame,
\par Kindling new from undefield
\par Ancient altars of the child.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Brothers, whom the wider life
\par Summons to a man's endeavour,
\par Bear our blessing to the strife,
\par Comrades once and comrades for ever:
\par Yours and ours, one saving star,
\par Here and on your fields afar,
\par Lightens from beside the throne,
\par Where the one Lord makes us one.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

